%N A023570 Greatest exponent in prime-power factorization of prime(n)-3; a(1) = a(2) = 0.
%H A023570 Amiram Eldar, <a href="/A023570/b023570.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a>
%F A023570 a(n) = A051903(A086801(n)) for n >= 3. - _Amiram Eldar_, Sep 26 2026
%F A023570 Asymptotic mean: Limit_{m->oo} (1/m) * Sum_{k=1..m} a(k) = 1 + Sum_{i>=1} (1 - Product_{p prime != 3} (1 - 1/((p-1)*p^i))) = 2.0655805829934496950028... . - _Amiram Eldar_, Oct 02 2026
%t A023570 Join[{0,0},Table[Max[FactorInteger[p-3][[All,2]]],{p,Prime[Range[3,100]]}]] (* _Harvey P. Dale_, Mar 11 2019 *)
%o A023570 (PARI) a(n) = if(n < 3, 0, vecmax(factor(prime(n)-3)[,2])); \\ _Amiram Eldar_, Sep 26 2026
%Y A023570 Cf. A023577, A051903, A086801.
%K A023570 nonn,easy,changed
